    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1934" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">allex</span></b> , ĭcis,
		m., acc. to Isid. Gloss., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the great toe;</i> hence, in derision, of a
			little man: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tune hic amator audes esse, allex viri?</span>”
				<i>thou thumb of a man</i>, <i>thumbling?</i>
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 5, 5, 31</span></i>
			.</div>
